course: dictionary
lesson: 13510
title: A rare word in a story
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are rare. You will mostly find them in old books and stories, not in everyday talk. «The thief was immured in a dark dungeon.» Dungeon is a clue: a dungeon is a deep prison, so immured must mean shut away somewhere.
explain: Read the words around the new word and ask what would fit. «After the argument, Sam immured himself in his room all day.» Sam did not go out or see anyone, so immured himself must mean shut himself away from other people.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence to check it. Put "shut away" in place of immured: «After the argument, Sam shut away himself in his room all day.» It is a bit clumsy, but the meaning is clear, so you know you have it right.
fact: Immure is a verb, so it describes an action: to immure someone, or to immure yourself.
fact: «Immure» means to shut someone up in a prison or a closed place, as if behind walls.
fact: «Immure» can also mean to shut yourself away from other people.
fact: Immure is a formal, old-fashioned word, so you will mostly meet it in books and stories.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad is immured in the deepest dungeon of the oldest castle in England for stealing a motor-car.
exercise: «The thief was immured in a dark dungeon.» What does immured mean? | *Shut away in a prison or closed place | Given a big meal | Let go free | Painted bright colours
exercise: «After the argument, Sam immured himself in his room all day.» What does Sam do? | Goes out to play football | Cleans the whole house | Invites friends round for tea | *Shuts himself away from other people
exercise: In «The knight was immured in the tower, far from the sun.», which word means shut away? | *immured | sun | knight | tower
test: Toad is immured in a dungeon in The Wind in the Willows. What does immured mean here? | Lost in a forest | Let out to play in the castle gardens | Invited to a feast | *Shut up in a closed place, like a prison
test: «Lily immured herself in her bedroom and would not talk to anyone.» What does this show? | She was hosting a party | She was lost and afraid of the dark | *She wanted to be alone, away from others | She was very hungry
exam: Read this: «The old prisoner was immured for twenty years.» What does this tell you? | *He was kept shut away in a prison for a long time | He was chosen to be king | He was let out early for good behaviour | He travelled the world as a sailor
